ow  does she feel about seeing herself on  the big screen in her first feature film  well not her first but at least first in  the leading role I remember she was in I  am loved I think yes yes yes no it's her  first big big role and she has seen the  film I think she's now seen it three  times because I wanted her to see it on  her own to start off with to to  experience it because it's a big deal  when you see yourself I don't know what  it feels like actually but I can imagine  it's a big deal sitting yourself on the  screen for the first time  and and then Tom also saw it ahead of  Sundance because I didn't want either of  them to see the film for the first time  here that's yeah can you identify that  with that at all do you like watching  yours I mean maybe not like watching  yourself on screen but do you like to  watch your films especially before  premieres ticket there's so many other  thoughts kick in while you're watching  yourself so it's quite hard to just sit  back and yeah but I think you know I as  testament to the film when you are able  to do that and I really certainly the  first time I saw it was just completely  kind of absorbed in it and obviously the  second time there's an audience so it's  a little different and you both went  into the screening last night with it  being public knowledge that you're  shooting the sequel this summer so just  curious  were you kind of waiting nervously for  the reaction out of this part knowing  that you're already teed up to go make  another movie I didn't think of it  exactly in that way but I haven't looked  at anything written about the film from  last night because I don't want to find  I'm reading something a reaction to the  first one that will make me  self-conscious about anything I do in  the second one because I think that the  sort of name of the game really is is is  freedom taking risks I don't consider  them really risk but I just want to be  able to play and not think about what  somebody said 